<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arnulf of Carinthia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 850–899</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arnulf of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a> was an illegitimate Carolingian who deposed his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat">Charles the Fat</a> in 887 and became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a>. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dyle">Dyle</a> in 891, fought Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> and was crowned emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 896. He made his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwentibold">Zwentibold</a> king of Lotharingia in 895. After his death <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyar</a> raids devastated the kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia.jpg" alt="Arnulf of Carinthia" width="236" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Arnulph_of_Carinthia_(896).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
